# project.done

Completed: 2026-09-15 (THE FINAL BLITZ lane; release v0.9.10, commit
7825f8d, tag v0.9.10 pushed with CI green).

## What shipped

The 2026-09-13 final audit's ranked list, executed top-down in the one
release: the decorator-count HIGH restated as wording (the spelling named,
admin's wrapper protections noted, dated errata on the 0.9.9 and 0.7.0 and
0.5.0 entries under the inline-errata policy); the Bootstrap dropdown menu
themed (the last stock-white surface; latent until a 2+-format book
exists); the cover read tick re-pinned to the Glyphicon font; check-theme
hardened (148 named colours, modern notations, raw-hex-outside-:root,
--mono lead, brace/var sanity, rendered logo derivatives with a graceful
tool skip, and a --selftest that reintroduces every bypass) and verified by
live reintroduction; the ledger's missing page-count/reader-state rows and
the spec amendment batch (contrast truth, /basic note with decision #106,
caliBlur wording, radius exception, grid-series register, write-guard
breadth, series-ledger contract line, venv reword, apostrophe seam,
Canadian spelling recorded); fork touches under grant #117 (series
double-render fix, read-guard dead branch, vendored sheet; suite 86 green);
the GitHub batch (Releases for v0.9.7/0.9.8/0.9.9 verbatim, README
screenshots hotlink, description clause, topic swap, wiki off); the CI
fork checkout (icon byte-diff runs on CI; coupling approved) plus action
bumps to v7; the compound `just sync`, the inert default recipe, the
report-only selector linter; the .gitignore prune; and the 1.0.0
agent-executable prep (workspace-map row updated).

Gates answered and executed: push (standing blitz grant), v0.9.7 Release
published as-is (the recorded em-dash stands in the immutable tag), GitHub
batch GO (full scope), CI coupling GO, historical-correction policy =
inline dated errata, spelling = Canadian English, .gitignore pruned.

